{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider was neither silent nor uncontactable, and the driver left the exchange hanging. The chat log records the driver's message 'hi im at the pickup point, where are you' at 19:59:12 (read by the rider at 19:59:52) and the rider's reply 'coming down now' at 20:01:07 - sent inside the waiting window that opened with the driver's arrival at 19:58:47 and closed at termination at 20:06:00. Under POL-NS-04 limbs (a) and (b) that reply is a coordinating message, and the driver neither posted any reply within 120 seconds of it (his only message predates it) nor placed any in-app voice call before terminating the trip: trip_record.in_app_calls is empty. This is the coordination failure the clause is aimed at, and the rider did everything limbs (a) and (b) ask of him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02701", "EV-TRIP-02701"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not press exoneration under POL-NS-04 and does not ask the Judge to treat limb (c) as satisfied, because the rider's own trace reports the rider's device between 884.0 m and 891.3 m from the pickup pin and motionless throughout (every rider fix at 0.0 km/h), and the code reports rider_qualifying_fix_count as 0 - so the 100 m STANDARD presence radius is not made out on the rider's own reported positions. The rider concedes that limb rather than stretch it. If the zero qualifying count reflects the 25 m accuracy filter rather than distance - no horizontal-accuracy value for any rider fix is exposed in the brief - limb (c) is undecidable under POL-NS-11 and the Judge should say the test could not be run rather than inferring the rider was elsewhere; that distinction is the only thing the rider asks the Judge to hold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02701"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this pickup road in this window. EV-ADVIS-02701-01 is MISSING - a blocking MISSING_ARTIFACT issue, admissibility weight 0.0 - and its absence is itself citable. Under POL-NS-06 limb (i) a traffic_advisory must be present and populated before separate in-geofence intervals may be summed, so the driver cannot extend the measured dwell by accumulation; any dwell finding must rest on the single continuous run the trace actually contains, and nothing may be added to it from an absent artifact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02701-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.run_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "This ruling concerns the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02701. The fee stands, and the platform pays the driver SGD 3.60. To the rider: your account that you were only a few minutes late is not accepted on the record. To the driver: your no-show is established and your compensation is fixed.\n\nThe no-show is proved on all four limbs of POL-NS-01, each on full-weight evidence. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 19:58:47. (b) The GPS trace places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at that moment: the closest fix is 0.16 m from the pin and there are 44 qualifying in-geofence fixes, so the POL-NS-02 test of at least three consecutive in-radius fixes at 25 m accuracy or better is met. (c) The driver held position continuously for 429 seconds (19:58:47 to 20:05:56), measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix as the clause requires rather than from the arrival tap, which is 249 seconds longer than the 180-second free waiting period in trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec. (d) The driver terminated the trip at 20:06:00 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, 253 seconds after the required dwell elapsed at 20:01:47, with no boarding event and no started trip. The arrival marker was true - the driver was on the pin and stationary, so neither the 300 m nor the 15 km/h trigger of POL-NS-05 fires - and nothing is recomputed.\n\nThe rider's account is contradicted by his own device track, which places him between 884 m and 891 m from the pickup pin and motionless (0.0 km/h) throughout the waiting window, with 0 of 62 fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius. POL-NS-04 therefore does not exonerate him: his 'coming down now' message at 20:01:07 went unanswered by the driver within 120 seconds and no in-app call was made, satisfying limbs (a) and (b), but limb (c) is affirmatively failed. This is not the undecidable case of POL-NS-11: the rider track is present (62 fixes with measured distances), and the failure is on distance (884 m), not on the 25 m accuracy filter, so the test could be run and it failed.\n\nThe other rider-side routes are checked. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) is not engaged, because the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, not outside it. POL-NS-06 (waiting-period shortfall) is not engaged, because the 429-second dwell exceeds the 180-second minimum by 249 seconds. Traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02701-01 is MISSING (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0), which makes the accumulation limb POL-NS-06(i) unavailable; accumulation was never needed, and an absent advisory neither reduces the required minimum nor counts against the driver.\n\nOn integrity there is no defect under POL-NS-08: the arrival event and the first in-geofence fix share the same second, the trace has 100% coverage with no gap, the chat log holds the two messages the trip record counts, and the SGD 4.50 fare line reconciles to the platform-policy figure. The deciding facts - arrival and dwell - are carried by EV-TRIP-02701 and EV-GPS-02701, both at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor, and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires.\n\nOn the money: with POL-NS-01 satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, the fee stands and POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80% of the SGD 4.50 net fee in force, i.e. SGD 3.60 (the residual SGD 0.90 is retained as the platform service fee; the gross figure of SGD 6.61 is not used). The anti-farming check does not trip - driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0, below the threshold of 4 - so compensation is paid. The ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and, per POL-GEN-03, amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 as driver_compensation_sgd: it is the amount the ruling moves, not a refund, and the rider's charge stands. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so it executes automatically on issue. No clause produces a referral. This ruling is provisional; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "The SGD 4.50 no-show fee stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.60 of it. THIS RULING IS ADDRESSED TO BOTH PARTIES.\n\nDriver's case (accepted). Every limb of POL-NS-01 holds. (a) The trip record EV-TRIP-02701 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 19:58:47. (b) The GPS trace EV-GPS-02701 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at that moment: the derived arrival reports 44 qualifying in-geofence fixes, well over POL-NS-02's three consecutive in-radius fixes at 25 m accuracy or better, with a nearest approach of 0.16 m. (c) The driver held position for a single continuous in-geofence run of 429 seconds, 19:58:47 to 20:05:56, against the 180-second free waiting period in trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; the derived shortfall is -249 seconds, i.e. the period was exceeded by 249 seconds, and platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec is null so no longer threshold applies. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 20:06:00 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, 253 seconds after the required dwell elapsed at 20:01:47, and there is no boarding event. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee: the stationary fixes lie inside the radius, so POL-NS-03 is not engaged; the arrival marker was not false (the driver was on the pin at 0.16 m and stationary at 19:58:47, so neither the 300 m nor the 15 km/h trigger of POL-NS-05 fires); and the dwell exceeded the minimum, so POL-NS-06 is not engaged. Under POL-NS-07 the driver's compensation is 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee in force, SGD 3.60, which is the figure the fare breakdown's own money derivation (EV-FARE-02701) states. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0, below the threshold of 4, so the conjunctive test never reaches its rate limb.\n\nRider's case. I accept that the rider sent a coordinating message, 'coming down now', at 20:01:07, and that the driver posted no reply within 120 seconds of it and placed no in-app voice call (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty) — POL-NS-04 limbs (a) and (b) are made out. But limb (c) is affirmatively FAILED, not undecidable: the rider's own track places his device between 884 m and 891 m from the pickup pin (mean 888 m) throughout the waiting window, far outside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius. Because a distance is reported, this is a test that ran and failed on the rider's own positions, not a test that could not be run; POL-NS-11's undecidability provision does not apply and I do not infer the rider was elsewhere — his own device says he was ~888 m away. POL-NS-04 therefore cannot exonerate him, and the dispute falls to POL-NS-01. His account that he was 'only a few minutes late' is contradicted by the chat log and by his own trace. I also accept the rider's POL-NS-06 point that the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02701-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) makes the accumulation limb POL-NS-06(i) unavailable, so no intervals may be summed; it changes nothing, because the dwell is already a single continuous run longer than the minimum, and a MISSING artifact carries no fact either way.\n\nConfidence and integrity. Confidence is 0.9. Every artifact that carries a deciding fact — EV-TRIP-02701, EV-GPS-02701, EV-CHAT-02701 and EV-FARE-02701 — is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is not reduced. No POL-NS-08 limb is engaged: the fare line reconciles at SGD 4.50 against platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, the 19:58:47 arrival event matches the first qualifying GPS fix in the same second (zero skew, against the 90-second limit), the trace has 100 percent coverage and no gaps, and the chat log matches trip_record.chat_message_count. The only impaired artifact is the MISSING advisory at weight 0.0, which carries no fact this ruling relies on.\n\nNo POL-NS-09 trigger is present (no contradictory artifacts, no cross-party no-show pattern, no anti-farming trip), so no referral arises and the case is not escalated. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the ruling executes automatically. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
